+# Usage and what you pay for
+
+Kind: operating guide for a paying customer. It states the one thing that is
+measured, everything that is not, where your own usage is, and how a retry
+after a failure avoids being measured twice.
+
+[Searching and retrieving](service-searching-and-retrieving.md) shows the
+requests and answers that produce a measured unit. This page is the shorter
+answer to the question people ask first, which is what this will cost.
+
+## One measured unit is one downloaded item
+
+```text
+What the service measures
+├── Measured
+│   └── a body read the service accepted and recorded, one unit, named provisioned_item
+└── Never measured
+    ├── searching, at /api/v1/retrieval or through the intelligence_search tool
+    ├── discovering and listing what this account may see
+    ├── a manifest, including its digest, size and licence
+    ├── any refusal that happens before the body is released
+    ├── reading this account's own usage
+    └── a repeat of a body read that carries the same request_id
+```
+
+The service states this itself rather than leaving it to a document. The
+discover answer carries `never_metered`, and the four entries it lists are
+listing authorized items, a manifest with digests and sizes, a refusal before
+metering, and reading the tenant's own usage. It also carries `metered_unit`,
+which is `provisioned_item`.
+
+An item that is a package of several files is still one item. In a release
+that includes catalogue releases, every file of one package fetched with the
+same `request_id` is recorded once, as one unit. Release 16 and every earlier
+release do not read that request shape.
+[Searching and retrieving](service-searching-and-retrieving.md#one-file-of-a-package)
+shows the request.
+
+## The plan
+
+One paid plan, named Baltor Pro, at 29.00 US dollars each month, paid in US
+dollars. There is no annual price, no seat price and no second tier at launch.
+Search is free. There is no overage billing at launch. An invited account is
+free, through an operator grant rather than a payment.
+
+## Before you download, the manifest tells you whether it will be measured
+
+A manifest is free, and it answers both of the questions that matter before a
+download. Ask for one, with the identity your search returned in place of
+`ITEM_IDENTITY`:
+
+```bash
+curl -sS -X POST https://app.baltor.ai/api/v1/provisioning \
+  -H "Authorization: Bearer $BALTOR_SERVICE_TOKEN" \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"record_type": "service_provisioning_request/v1",
+       "operation": "manifest", "identity": "ITEM_IDENTITY"}'
+```
+
+| Field in the answer | What it tells you |
+|---|---|
+| `body_allowed` | Whether this account, with this credential, may download the body at all. |
+| `metering_policy` | `required` when a successful download records one unit. `unmetered` when it does not. |
+| `size_bytes` | How large the body is, before you fetch it. |
+
+Those are the only two policy values. A `metering_policy` the service does not
+define is refused rather than guessed.
+
+## Where your usage is
+
+Reading your own usage is free and needs the `usage:read` scope.
+
+```bash
+curl -sS -H "Authorization: Bearer $BALTOR_SERVICE_TOKEN" \
+  https://app.baltor.ai/api/v1/usage
+```
+
+The answer is a `durable_tenant_usage/v1` record with exactly four fields
+beside its record type:
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `tenant_id` | The account these numbers belong to. |
+| `records` | How many measured body reads are recorded for this account. |
+| `totals` | The same count grouped by unit, so `{"provisioned_item": 10.0}` means ten downloaded items. |
+| `durability` | `durable` when the count is written to durable storage. |
+
+This is the authoritative count. It is not an estimate and it is not delayed
+by a reporting window. Read it before you repeat anything that downloads a
+body.
+
+The same numbers appear on `/account` in the browser, for the account you are
+signed in as.
+
+## Retrying without being measured twice
+
+Every body read carries a `request_id` that you choose. It identifies one
+download attempt.
+
+```text
+A download that failed with an uncertain outcome
+├── Repeat it with the SAME request_id
+│   ├── You get the same bytes
+│   └── No second unit is recorded
+└── Use a NEW request_id
+    └── This is a second measured read, on purpose
+```
+
+That rule is what makes the three uncertain refusals safe to handle:
+
+| Code | Status | What it means | What to do |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `meter_commit_unknown` | 503 | The unit may or may not have been recorded. | Retry with the same `request_id`. |
+| `deadline_exceeded` | 504 | The operation did not finish in time. Work may still be running. | Read `/api/v1/usage`, or retry with the same `request_id`. |
+| `commit_unknown` | 503 | A durable write was attempted and its outcome is unknown. | Read the current state before acting. |
+
+None of these means the work failed. Read first, act second.
+
+## When a download is accepted, the answer says so
+
+An inline read at `/api/v1/provisioning` returns the body inside a
+`provisioning_body/v2` record together with its metering acknowledgment, which
+is a `provisioning_meter_acknowledgment/v1` record. Read three fields from it:
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `metered` | Whether this particular read recorded a unit. |
+| `metered_unit` | `provisioned_item`, or absent when nothing was recorded. |
+| `metering_acknowledgment` | Carries `committed` and `durability`. |
+
+`durability` has three possible values, `volatile`, `durable` and `unknown`.
+`durable` means the record is written to durable storage. `unknown` means the
+service cannot state the outcome, which is the same situation as
+`meter_commit_unknown` and is handled the same way.
+
+## Two failures that are about the meter, not about you
+
+| Code | Status | Meaning | What to do |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `meter_unavailable` | 400 | The item requires metering and the meter is not installed on this host. | Report it to your operator. Nothing you send changes it. |
+| `meter_commit_unknown` | 503 | The unit may or may not have been recorded. | Retry with the same `request_id`. |
+
+A refusal before the body is released is never measured. That includes every
+credential, permission, request-shape, size and rate refusal in
+[the complete refusal table](service-serving-and-connections.md).
+
+## What the service does not measure
+
+- It does not measure the size of a body. One downloaded item is one unit
+  whether it is 300 bytes or the largest body the host will deliver.
+- It does not measure a search, however many results it returns.
+- It does not measure model calls, because it does not make any. Your model
+  spending is with your provider and never reaches this service.
+- It does not measure whether you used the material. A download is a download.
+
+## Related pages
+
+- [Searching and retrieving](service-searching-and-retrieving.md)
+- [Your account](service-your-account.md)
+- [Troubleshooting](service-troubleshooting.md)
+- [Billing setup and pricing](billing-setup-and-pricing.md), for the
+  engineering record behind the price
